rting him in the past while jeno says  she needs to equip some apology  functionality  absolutely love that conversation back  to back these two  are about to take on countless dragon  level teletubbies when fury ugly returns  grosser than ever  not only does he look worse as he's  melting he smells horribly too  he's after revenge against silver fang  and he's deadlier than ever  as his melting skin burns you may expect  darkshine's polished skin to be  resistant but no it burns like crazy to  his horror  ugly is releasing strong acid and can  even spit it  he brings s-class hero darkshine to the  ground so yeah darkshine has not had a  good day guys for an s-class hero with  garo first and now this  s-class truly doesn't mean much when the  villains are on this  level ugly also lets us know that the  acid is a result  of the digestive powers gums gave him so  it's like a super gross but op  fusion in a sense then we get one of the  darkest moments in the series up till  now  that includes zombie a member of the  council of swordsman he pretty much  served as a hero who would in theory  help atomic samurai handle garo  here he gets acid to his face and it's  bad half of his head is dissolved so he  pretty much has to be dead  and for one punch man having a good guy  like this horribly killed is a pretty  big move  it seems like with this chapter things  have definitely gotten darker  atomic samurai and nichiren attack and  all that happens is their swords melt  away  this does not look good for the heroes  all around we return to the fight  between garo and bomb  and bomb is clearly tired and sweating  all over the place  he's 83 so it makes sense that he  doesn't have the endurance of the young  garo  bomb lets us know that garo has combined  every technique and refined them into  his own style  still he is determined not to fail until  bang gets there  and launches an attack that is  surprisingly cancelled out by garro  garo knocks him out with an elbow as  bang 